<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4238" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăthămānĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθαμανία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A district in Epirus</i>, <i>on or
				near Mount Pindus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 36, 14</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăthămānes</span></b> ,
			um, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθαμᾶνες</span>, <i>the inhabitants of
				Athamania</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Pis. 40</span></i>; 
			<i><span class="en">Liv. 31,
				42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3, §
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăthă-mānis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>an Athamanian woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				311</span></i> Jahn.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăthămānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Athamania</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					5, 6, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
